    {
      "id": "d3b3c0de-0099-4000-8000-000000000101",
      "name": "Note 1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        200,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 760,
        "height": 360,
        "content": "## Monthly mail cleanup (Gmail personal + work + Outlook)\nSame 3 nodes per account, one after the other: **HTTP Request + pagination** lists ids matching `older_than:1y -in:trash` (500 per page, max 20 pages = 10,000 per run) → **Code** groups them by 1000 → **HTTP batchModify** adds the `TRASH` label (moves to Trash, not a permanent delete). Each chain uses its own **credential**.\nGmail empties Trash after 30 days → one month to recover anything.\n**Outlook** (Microsoft Graph): list ids with `@odata.nextLink` pagination (1000 per page, max 10 pages) → **Code** packs 20 `move` requests per **JSON $batch** call → *Deleted Items* (one call every 1.5 s, Outlook rate limits)."
      }
    }
